    description: "Found by the 2026-10-06 docstring staleness audit tail pass; reviewer reproduced: top-level const std = @import(\"std\") yields two identical edges (same id, merged downstream); inside a function const m = @import(\"mod\") yields two distinct edges, one from zig:c.zig:0-0:file:file and one from zig:c.zig:1-4:go:function. zig.py's module docstring now states the duplicate-edge gap."  # dd7a
    fields:  # dd7a
      statement: "One import construct produces one import edge, from a node that exists."  # dd7a
      root_cause: "The variable_declaration branch (~L477-500) emits the import edge, then falls through to push its children (~L597), so the builtin_function branch (~L502-520) emits another. Separately, the import edge src zig:<rel>:0-0:file:file (~L488) does not match the real file node id zig:<rel>:1-1:file:file, leaving a stray external_symbol node."  # dd7a
